This directory contains a few manually created fuzzers (fuzz_*.jkb.c)
and many LLM generated fuzzers, starting from my own fuzz_view.c as a
template.  Creating fuzzers for every subcommand is a long and tedious
task, so using an LLM (Claude in this case) to do that has been
beneficial.

The basic principle is that command line tools stress test the htslib
API more than it's own fuzzing (although more fuzzing is coming
there).  We can also validate the multitude of ways that CLI options
can interact.  So we generate data and a selected subset of command
line options per application, use this to build a samtools command
line, and then execute it in the usual way that bamtk() would.

WARNING: run the LLM code in a sandbox, maybe mine too!  I haven't
validated what they're doing is sane, and during development it became
obvious some things were initially escaping a bit.  Early fuzzers
didn't use -- for argument lists, meaning some fuzz mediated options
could be problematic (eg an LLM generated ref.fa with a region name
called "-o foo").  Some tools are inherently problematic too, such as
split by tag using tag contents in filenames.

The building is clunky.  It "works for me", but it's not designed as
production ready.  I just have various command lines put into .sh
files for compiling and linking.

We need to tidy this up, but it's at the case of minimal best efforts
so we can find and fix the problems at speed without spending time on
polish.  The aim being to head off the slew of AI generated issues and
PRs by getting ahead of the curve somewhat.  There will still be a lot
missed, but this has already proven it's worth as an easy starting
point.


Build Samtools/Htslib
---------------------

Build samtools and htslib with -fsanitize=fuzzer.  This will fail on command line
utilities, but we can ignore that.  (TODO: add a method of building the
object files without the executables.)

make -j8 CC="clang -fsanitize=address,undefined,fuzzer" CFLAGS="-g -DFUZZING_BUILD_MODE_UNSAFE_FOR_PRODUCTION" -k

You may want to have previously built a full samtools binary so we can
verify under valgrind.


Build the fuzzers
-----------------

Download the files.zip and unpack

Run build.sh with fuzzer=???.

build.sh is below:
#fuzzer=markdup
(CC=clang;cd ../..;$CC -I. -Ihtslib -fsanitize=address,undefined,fuzzer -g -DFUZZING_BUILD_MODE_UNSAFE_FOR_PRODUCTION -Dexit=fuzz_exit test/fuzz/fuzz_$fuzzer.c -L./lz4 bam_aux.o bam_index.o bam_plcmd.o sam_view.c bam_fastq.o bam_cat.o bam_md.o bam_plbuf.o bam_reheader.o bam_sort.o bam_rmdup.o bam_rmdupse.o bam_mate.o bam_stat.o bam_color.o bam2bcf.o sample.o cut_target.o phase.o bam2depth.o coverage.o padding.o bedcov.o bamshuf.o faidx.o dict.o stats.o stats_isize.o bam_flags.o bam_split.o bam_tview.o bam_tview_curses.o bam_tview_html.o bam_lpileup.o bam_quickcheck.o bam_addrprg.o bam_markdup.o tmp_file.o bam_ampliconclip.o amplicon_stats.o bam_import.o bam_samples.o bam_consensus.o consensus_pileup.o reference.o reset.o cram_size.o bam_checksum.o ./lz4/lz4.o libst.a htslib/libhts.a -lpthread -lz -lm -lbz2 -llzma -ldeflate -lcurl -lcrypto -lncursesw -lm -lz  -lpthread -o test/fuzz/fuzz_$fuzzer)

Run with:

for i in fuzz_*.c;do f=`echo $i | sed 's/fuzz_\(.*\)\.c$/\1/'`;fuzzer=$f bash build.sh;done


Create test infrastructure
--------------------------

Setup PATH to contain samtools binary.
Run the make_fuzz_data.py script to create fuzz_data directory.


Execute
-------

cd fuzz_data
fuzzer=depth bash ../setup.sh

# setup.sh is
#cp -r runtime runtime.$fuzzer
#cp -r seeds/$fuzzer runtime.$fuzzer/corpus


Then run it:
Change to detect_leaks=1 after fixing the more egregious issues first
Also add -dict=$fuzzer.dict if available

cd fuzz_data/runtime.$fuzzer
(for i in `seq 1 1000`;do ASAN_OPTIONS=allow_addr2line=1:abort_on_error=1:detect_leaks=0 ../../fuzz_$fuzzer -detect_leaks=0 corpus -rss_limit_mb=12560 -timeout=1 2>&1 ;done) | tee fuzz.out

Also see ../../run_fuzz.sh


Parallel
--------

for i in fuzz_*.c;do f=`echo $i | sed 's/fuzz_\(.*\)\.c$/\1/'`;export fuzzer=$f;echo fuzzing $fuzzer; (cd fuzz_data;bash ../setup.sh;cd runtime.$fuzzer;../../run_fuzz.sh) & done
